      {
        "id": "ben-ln-4",
        "name": "Pâte Rouge with Gboma Dessi",
        "difficulty": "Medium",
        "servings": 4,
        "prepTime": 20,
        "cookTime": 40,
        "ingredients": [
          "Pâte: 2 cups corn flour, water, palm oil (for color)",
          "Gboma dessi: 1 large bunch gboma (African spinach/eggplant leaf)",
          "Smoked fish or crab",
          "Palm oil",
          "Tomatoes, onion, garlic",
          "Scotch bonnet pepper",
          "Fermented locust beans (dawadawa/soumbala)",
          "Salt"
        ],
        "instructions": [
          "Make the sauce: blend tomatoes, onion, pepper",
          "Fry in palm oil until sauce darkens and oil floats",
          "Add smoked fish or crab, dawadawa",
          "Add chopped gboma leaves, simmer until wilted",
          "For the pâte: bring water to boil with a splash of palm oil",
          "Add corn flour gradually, stirring hard with a wooden spoon",
          "Cook and stir until thick, smooth, and pulls away from pot",
          "Mold pâte into a ball, serve in bowl with sauce ladled over",
          "Eat with your right hand — pinch off pâte, scoop sauce"
        ],
        "description": "The cornerstone of Beninese home cooking — smooth corn pâte with a rich, funky gboma leaf sauce spiked with dawadawa (fermented locust beans) and smoked crab. West African food creators have made pâte-and-sauce videos some of the most shared content from Francophone Africa."
      }
